  "text": "Créd is a fairy queen of the Irish tales. The twin hills of Munster, called the Paps of Danu, carry her story. A man had to praise her hidden palace in verse, without ever seeing it, to win her, and the poet-seer Cáel met that test. She dressed him in a magic coat of war, yet he fell while serving his king, and Créd cast herself into his grave. She also wrote verse, and one of her songs is kept in the Colloquy of the Elders. A second woman of that name, a daughter of king Guaire, counts among the ancestors of the O'Connors. She loved the wandering poet Cano Mac Gartnáin, guarded his pledge, and in her ruin broke the stone of his soul, whereupon Cano died too.",
